// Title: Chopper Webshell Process Pattern
// Sigma ID: fa3c117a-bc0d-416e-a31b-0c0e80653efb
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), MSTI (query)
// Date: 2022-10-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, discovery, T1505.003, T1018, T1033, T1087
// Description: Detects patterns found in process executions cause by China Chopper like tiny (ASPX) webshells
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/09/30/analyzing-attacks-using-the-exchange-vulnerabilities-cve-2022-41040-and-cve-2022-41082/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_webshell_chopper.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\w3wp.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\w3wp.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "&ipconfig&echo" or ProcessCommandLine contains "&quser&echo" or ProcessCommandLine contains "&whoami&echo" or ProcessCommandLine contains "&c:&echo" or ProcessCommandLine contains "&cd&echo" or ProcessCommandLine contains "&dir&echo" or ProcessCommandLine contains "&echo [E]" or ProcessCommandLine contains "&echo [S]")
